eldon ring  a couple weeks ago i made a quick  trailer breakdown for gamespot based on  my initial impressions of alden ring's  exciting gameplay reveal from summer  game fest  since then a lot has happened hidetaka  miyazaki has revealed a plethora of new  information through various interviews  so i'd love to break down what we know  so far about the game into further  detail  especially since all the gameplay we've  seen so far has been re-contextualized  thanks to these interviews  let's start with the solo gameplay in an  interview for famitsu magazine  translated by the angry furlong on  reddit miyazaki revealed that the game  will feature a heavy amount of  customization  and lots of ways to tackle dangerous  situations in the game  the game borrows heavily from gameplay  mechanics of from software's dark souls  series  in particular and while the game could  very well have been dark souls 4  miyazaki and team wanted the freedom of  a brand new world in ip but there are  still  plenty of things that are borrowed from  dark souls including the fact that  you're playing a nameless character who  you create and customize the appearance  of  elden bling here we come  there will also be a large variety of  weapons and spells both of which we saw  showcased in the trailer  but something unique will be the way  elden ring handles weapon arts  which were first introduced in dark  souls 3.  in dark souls 3 weapon arts were special  attacks that were tied to a specific  weapon  however in elden ring these weapons will  be separate skills you're able to  somehow  gain and collect every weapon has one  weapon art slot and you customize your  weapon by equipping a weapon art to it  according to miyazaki there will be  around 100 weapons that you'll be able  to obtain  another added element to the way you can  tackle enemy encounters  comes in the form of spirits you can now  summon while the specifics of this  mechanic are still a little fuzzy to me  we saw it showcased in the gameplay  trailer when the player character  crushes a cube  in the souls games the markers for  cooperative npc  phantoms you could summon to help you in  battles would appear on the ground  and you had to meet certain conditions  like not being hollow  in order to be allowed to summon certain  characters like soleir  i'm not certain yet how to gain spirits  but what i do know is that they're going  to be  according to miyazaki basically based on  enemies  so does that mean it's like pokemon  where you trap a weakened enemy  into a cube and now it's your ally  finally the dark souls pokemon game  we've all been waiting for  and by we i mean me kind of be like  persona 5  in a way if you think about it but there  are so many possibilities for how you  might gain these spirits that i don't  feel good about fully speculating on it  the spirits are an extremely interesting  addition though  because they're essentially another  weapon and tool at your disposal  they act like weapons armor or magic  that you equip to your character  and interestingly just like a weapon you  can even level up these individual  spirits  however similar to summoning a phantom  in dark souls you're only allowed to  summon these spirits in certain places  they widely vary from shield characters  who protect you to archers that'll aid  you in the back line  decoys and more according to miyazaki  there are even some spirits will be  pretty much  useless so i'm just imagining the  pendant from dark souls being a spirit  you summon that just falls in the grass  and does nothing  you then leveled up to 100 hoping it'll  be like magikarp  and it just sits there taunting you  another new yet familiar element will be  stealth  stealth was of course first introduced  in and a major part of from software's  last game  securo and this mechanic will be making  a return for eldon ring allowing you to  approach a dangerous situation in a  completely different way  and i have to imagine it'll make  backstabs a whole lot easier to  accomplish  and speaking of which we have  confirmation that parrying enemies will  be back  another gameplay element first  introduced in securo and making its way  over at elder ring  is jumping jumping was a critical  feature of battle and securo and it  sounds like it will work in a similar  way in elder ring  allowing you to jump over low sweeping  attacks i do wonder what that means for  dodging in iframes if jumping is a  viable means of countering your enemies  in the trailer we do see a couple  moments where it looks clear that the  player is dodging away and  i-frames are saving them later on in the  trailer the wolf-like boss shoots a  magic beam at the player and the player  dodges it by dashing through the beam  which looks like it's straight out of  bloodborne again the dodge and iframe  save the player character from injury  immediately after the wolf like boss  performs a low sweeping attack  and this time the player character  chooses to jump over it instead of  dashing through it  so i think it's clear that dodging and  iframes will work the exact  same way they did in dark souls the  question is  are there certain attacks you'll only be  able to properly dodge by jumping  it's definitely going to be interesting  to see how important jumping is from a  defensive perspective  from an offensive perspective you can  now jump for a heavy attack  there is a shot at the end of the elder  ring trailer which shows the player  jumping and striking at one of the  game's demigod bosses  admittedly on first watching the trailer  i thought this was just something  cinematic they were showing  but after reading miyazaki's interview  it's clear that this is a strike the  player can perform  miyazaki also compared the combat of  elder ring to sekiro and its  resurrection mechanic  while eldon ring will not feature  resurrection mechanic which allows  players to feel a sense of progression  and progress without ruining their  gameplay rhythm eldon ring will feature  similar elements to keep players engaged  and allow for a sense of meta  progression  something i found extremely notable from  an ign interview with hitake miyazaki  was a statement about the stamina bar  something that has been a prominent  feature of souls and derivative souls  like games  according to miyazaki the stamina bar  exists in elder ring  but we feel it has less influence on the  player overall  we wanted to make it feel less  restrictive and contribute to that level  of freedom more so than our previous  titles one of the game's major additions  will be horseback riding  and yes i realize they look like yakults  from princess mononoke  but for the time being horseback riding  is the term he's been using in  interviews  we see a number of battles take place on  horseback this includes one against what  looks to be a more normal enemy and one  against a dragon  as we see this horseback boss battle  against the dragon in the trailer i do  wonder if you're limited to only using  your horse in certain scenarios in the  game  miyazaki has stated that in multiplayer  you won't be able to travel on horseback  so here's what i think might be the case  as miyazaki has stated there's a large  open field you traverse via horse and  in your travels you'll find six larger  vertically designed dungeon areas known  as legacy dungeons  perhaps once you reach a legacy dungeon  you're no longer allowed to call your  horse  this would mean that for any boss or  enemy you find in the open field  your horse is another tool and way to  fight there will also be smaller  abandoned villages and runes and you'll  find bosses in some of these you can use  your horse to fight as well  in his fumitsu interview miyazaki stated  travel on horseback will be limited to  the open field but i think it really  feels nice  so this would make sense to me and  speaking of which in the battle against  the dragon  there's a scene where you don't just  jump once but double jump in mid  air so it's clear that the horse will  have unique skills not just for  traversing the world's terrain  but even for battle unlike previous from  software games  you'll be able to craft and customize  items in elder ring from various  materials you find in the world  miyazaki states that while there will be  more resources for you to recover your  health this time around  as you'll be fighting for longer than in  previous games presumably  in between other checkpoints hp recovery  will still be handled in a special way  comparable to previous titles when it  comes to overall difficulty of elder  ring  miyazaki compares it to dark souls 3.  like the spirits i was mentioning you  don't have to rely on pure mechanical  skill  but can use strategy to defeat your  enemies we are emphasizing a strategic  approach to combat in this game  this leads me nicely into multiplayer  we have official confirmation that there  will be cooperative gameplay and pvp  within  eldon ring when it comes to cooperative  multiplayer the game has been further  expanded to allow players to create  groups  these groups will have a special  appearance and are matched via password  and a group can be of an unlimited size  at least for the time being  all of this to me sounds like it means  from software is going to allow clans  within elden ring  it will be prioritized in matchmaking  with any group you set  so if you want to create a kirk fan club  a la iron pineapple  it sounds like you'll be able to quickly  match with your friends far more easily  than in any previous souls game  that said beyond this it's hard to say  if there will be any additional  functionality for these groups beyond  easier matchmaking  overall the co-op will function  similarly to dark souls and summon signs  with players only able to be summoned in  certain areas and then being booted out  after defeating a boss  something that some players struggled  with in securo was that unlike the souls  games there weren't too many options for  progressing in the game beyond getting  better at the game's core mechanics  with alden ring miyazaki will be keeping  the relative difficulty of the game  similar to souls but including many ways  for players who are less skilled  mechanically to progress  including this element of cooperative  play with other online players  and while co-op has existed in every  souls game including demon souls  miyazaki hopes to lower the barrier of  entry for this element of the game  in order to do this elder ring will  limit how many resources are necessary  for multiplayer  and you'll no longer need to use a  semi-rare resource like humanity in  order to summon  while there aren't too many details  about the pvp as of yet  we do have confirmation that it will  exist thanks to an interview with the  russian website egromania  translated by calibrono and sulky bat on  reddit  apparently miyazaki was noticeably  excited to talk about the pvp  and says there will be both invasions  and optional pvp  he also stated the team is working to  make pvp less irritating for both  players  hopefully that means we'll actually get  some kind of pvp arena in the vanilla  game  he also specifically mentioned trying to  add certain information so pvp wouldn't  just be an endless game of hide and seek  i have to imagine that thanks to the  sheer amount of customization for player  builds within elder ring  pvp will thrive in this game especially  if groups are matched with other groups  of similar sizes  finally while there will be a return of  covenants in the alden ring miyazaki  specifically compared it to demon souls  which uh has no covenants in this regard  he said there's no minimum requirement  for multiplayer and that while covenants  will return there are more so for role  playing and to spice things up  my personal favorite map design of any  from software game has been  dark souls the game has an interwoven  world and it's a blast discovering  every major shortcut and way to progress  from one area to another  however every game has handled traversal  in a slightly different manner  because there was no warping in dark  souls until the latter half of the game  this interwoven map design was  incredibly important to making traversal  less of a slog  and much more of a reward demon souls  and bloodborne both featured a main hub  with warping to distinct and separate  disconnected major areas  those areas were often times interwoven  within themselves but fairly distinct  meanwhile dark souls 2 and 3 allowed for  warping right off the bat  from one checkpoint to another this  meant that the overall maps weren't as  interwoven  but had distinct branches that would jut  out while miyazaki has stated that there  will  indeed be a hub area players won't be  able to access at the start of the game  but can eventually gain access to i  think elder ring will be completely  distinct in this regard  according to miyazaki the overall world  design will feel more like a classic rpg  the open field of the game serves to  expand the scale of the story  increasing immersion there is a great  unknown  and threat in this world and there's a  thrill of feeling your way through the  world intended to bring the joy of  discovery and travel  i think this is one of the joys that the  old classic rpgs had  and we wanted to aim for that in this  game there is what you would call a  world map for the open field areas  you can set a waypoint travel to  uncharted areas and enjoy revealing the  map  on the other hand as in the dark souls  series there is  no map in the big dungeon areas we want  you to enjoy figuring out the layout  through exploration  and to have that great feeling when you  finally do so it seems like there's a  large  exterior world map similar perhaps to a  classic jrpg-like final fantasy  or maybe even skyrim or breath of the  wild that you explore with your horse  here unlike any other modern from  software game you'll actually have a map  that you'll uncover as you discover new  locations  according to miyazaki besides the  extremely thought out vertical legacy  dungeons  there are many small to medium scale  dungeon areas  forts catacombs caves mining tunnels etc  we are planning to have many npcs but  currently there are no towns or villages  where they reside  there are places that were once villages  but are now abandoned and the prowling  places of dangerous enemies  so i imagine that all of these smaller  to medium scale dungeons  forts and the rest are a part of this  larger map and area you traverse on  horse  to my mind it will probably be somewhat  like my previous examples of breath of  the wild or skyrim  however once you find a legacy dungeon  the area within is a much more like a  classic dark souls dungeon  so imagine you're traversing along the  world and you stumble upon the tower of  latria  once you enter latria you no longer have  a map and you'll have to explore  just like you did in demon souls i'm not  sure how you enter these legacy dungeons  and if it will be something like a large  castle you'll stumble upon that you'll  explore  or if it's something you warp to  something i brought attention to in my  trailer breakdown video was  this scene of a hand grabbing a naked  character who i think is the player  initially i thought this was something  from the beginning of the game and how  you enter the lands between  i still think that's likely the case but  it's worth mentioning that a similar  mechanic could just be how you enter  into legacy dungeons  although i'd like to think every legacy  dungeon will be different both in style  and how you enter it  and can't wait to see how from software  will surprise us  further helping with this large scope of  the game elder ring will feature a fast  travel system  however we still don't know the exact  details of how this system will work  miyazaki has stated that you won't have  to defeat every boss in the game in  order to win  and that many of them are skippable  furthermore the order and timing of most  of the boss battles  is completely up to the player while the  dark souls games in particular  have always included elements of this  according to miyazaki this level of  freedom and order of progression will be  even more heightened in the elden ring  something relatively new to aid you in  traversing these areas is the ability to  jump  this is of course a mechanic that was  insecure but is now being introduced  into a much more standard souls-like  game  as i mentioned before the horse will be  able to jump which will aid you in  traversing the world  i imagine that means there will be many  hidden nooks for you to find in the  world and dangerous ledges you'll have  to try to jump  off of or land on to find hidden weapons  armor and more  additionally in the trailer we saw that  the horse can seem to jump straight up  certain cliffs  although notably before your horse does  this they actually jump off of a special  magical ring  so you'll probably be limited in the  specific ability to certain spots that  from software allows you to actually  launch from  in other words that rock creature with a  bell under it and building on top  you probably won't be able to just  launch up to the building unless  hitting the bell creates one of those  magical jumping rings who knows  miyazaki's hinted jumping will be a  major element to exploring legacy  dungeons and expressed that jumping as a  new dimension of freedom  perhaps especially players who played a  lot of dark souls series will find this  refreshing  while gravity was the number one op  enemy of dark souls  it seems that jumping has completely  changed the way falling and fall damage  will work  we've adjusted fall damage to make the  game less stressful considering that the  freedom allowed by jumping is an  important part of the game  we've made it so enemy attacks won't  cause you to fall unfairly and have  also adjusted the fall damage down  bandai namco's website  included this story dump and we get a  little more of a breakdown from hitataka  miyazaki  the background mythology of elder ring's  world was crafted by george r.r martin  which involves the lands between here a  race called the demigods have received  the blood of the divine queen marika  and are heroes that rule this land  having received a particularly powerful  blessing  all who receive this blessing have a  golden light in their eyes  but these people have lost this light  they are called tarnished because they  have lost this golden light from their  eyes  and are driven out of the lands between  the tarnished who is the protagonist of  the game is a descendant of the people  who were driven out of the lands between  and now when the elder ring which forms  the source of the blessing of the golden  tree has been shattered  this once lost blessing is returned to  the tarnished who reside outside the  lands between  it is a rumbling to become the king  which beckons you to the lands between  and to the elden ring in the trailer  we're told the tarnish will fight  or die in an unending curse so similar  to dark souls your character  a tarnished would seem to have an undead  curse upon them i find it likely that  part of this beckoning that calls your  character to the lands between  involves this particular shot of a hand  grabbing a character and taking them  away  your mission is to defeat the various  demigods who once heroes of the land  but grew mad with power after obtaining  a shard of the elder ring  you play as one of the many descendants  of the tarnished who lost their grace  and were exiled from the lands between  long long ago as miyazaki revealed in an  interview with ign  and that would indicate you aren't the  only tarnish who has been beckoned back  to the lands between  he states i feel like one of the main  themes of the game is how the player  the tarnished approaches or treats this  newfound grace and this return to the  land that they were once banished from  how they interpret this and the meaning  it's not just the player character of  course  it's lots of characters in the game who  are all beckoned back and will have  their own adventures and motives  we want the players to discover for  themselves what that means and how they  want to begin their adventure  while i'm sure that there will be plenty  of bosses as there are six  legacy dungeons and miyazaki has stated  that these are the domains of the major  demigod characters  that leads me to believe there will be a  total of 6 demigods  and it's my suspicion that many of these  demigods are those who we saw in the  original eldon ring trailer  i find it likely that the 2019 trailer  may have been footage from the intro  cinematic to the game  introducing the demigods of the world  the silver herod and crowned demigod  with multiple hands  is featured in the original trailer and  then prominently in the gameplay trailer  another one is the valkyrie-like  character who has a detachable arm  and who we see absolutely obliterating a  player character in the gameplay trailer  another character we see is a large  warrior with massive boar-like armor  who i can't find in the gameplay trailer  this looks to be straight from a  cutscene about the war that broke out  after the shattering  it's possible this character is either  dying from the war or  could be another one of the demigods  miyazaki has stated of these demigods  that  we wanted to depict these beings as not  just creatures and horrible monsters but  have an element of heroism  and an element of mythology to them  essentially they are the old gods of  this world  as the demigods were all heroes of their  time i find it strongly possible that  this particular night with wings in the  gameplay trailer is another one of the  major demigods  according to miyazaki part of the design  of these major characters  is that inheriting the shards of the  elder ring they each inherited  a different power or element so to speak  and each was twisted and warped in its  own way  and it brought a tainted strength to  each of them this  well describes why one of the demigods  has so many arms and i think that  could describe the wolf-like boss we see  in the gameplay trailer as well  who just might be another one of the six  demigods  one thing i still wonder about is the  blacksmith in the trailer  do you think it could be this character  from the gameplay trailer with  dreadlocks  i'm honestly not sure some more story  related details we know about elder ring  are that  for the most part the story will be told  more akin to the souls games or  bloodborne  with fragments the player will need to  piece together i'm personally a fan of  this style of storytelling and games  which is why i've made several from  software lore videos over the years  and i'm looking forward to discovering  an all new mythology this way  although for those of you who like the  story to be a little less obtuse  it does sound like the game's surface  level story will be a little easier to  understand  and possibly take some cues from the  storytelling of sekito  as with every modern from software game  there will be multiple endings to elden  ring this one deserves its own category  i'm sure we all fondly remember the  valley of defilement  blighttown harvest valley the nightmare  frontier  farron keep and the ocean and deaths  maybe even the big mine  the path of poison or mines filled with  bacon logs over poison  for my king's full bros out there ah yes  the best areas of any from software game  poison swamps the best  the best they're back we have  confirmation elder ring will have a  poison swamp  oh boy  [Music]  eldon ring releases january 21 2022.  let me know if there any details that  have you excited and what i might have  missed between this and my trailer  breakdown  if you enjoyed this video please  consider giving it a like and make sure  to stick to gamespot for more elton ring  i guarantee you that myself and to more  hussein will be incessantly talking  about elder ring the closer and closer  to release we get  and i'll see you guys next time  [Music]  foreign

